<Base title="Privacy | Tidewater" description="How Tidewater handles information sent through its website.">
<section class="section"><div class="container article legal"><h1>Privacy</h1><p class="fine">Effective November 5, 2026</p>
<p>Tidewater is a trade name of James C. Simpson III, a sole proprietor, 1708 A St SE, Washington, DC 20003 (<a href="mailto:hello@tidewaterbid.com">hello@tidewaterbid.com</a>).</p>
<h2>What we collect</h2><p>What you send us: name, organization, email, phone, location, project or service details, Opportunity Finder and readiness answers, the bid or program you ask about, your consent and its timestamp, and any message. If you email a résumé to career@tidewaterbid.com, we receive what you send.</p>
<h2>How we use it</h2><p>To reply, review funding programs or bids that may fit, scope and deliver any engagement, and follow up by email within the consent you gave. We do not sell your information or run a mailing list.</p>
<h2>Who processes it</h2><p>Cloudflare hosts the site, handles form submissions and spam screening, and routes our email. Airtable stores form submissions and purchase records. Stripe processes payments; we never see or store your full card or bank number. If analytics are enabled, Plausible counts visits without cookies or personal profiles. We share information otherwise only if the law requires it or you ask us to, such as with a funder or agency in an application you approve.</p>
<h2>Retention and your choices</h2><p>We keep inquiry records while they are useful for your request or engagement and delete them on request unless the law requires us to keep them. Résumés are kept no longer than 12 months. Email <a href="mailto:hello@tidewaterbid.com">hello@tidewaterbid.com</a> to see, correct or delete your information, or to stop follow-up email.</p>
<h2>Browser storage</h2><p>The site remembers your light or dark display setting in your browser. It uses no advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
<h2>Changes</h2><p>We will post any update here with a new effective date.</p>
</div></section>
</Base>
